<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Matthew Orsini</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 1195–1238</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Maio Orsini</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Matthew Orsini was the founder of the Orsini county palatine of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kefalonia">Cephalonia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zakynthos">Zakynthos</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ionian-sea">Ionian Sea</a>. Of an Apulian family, he held the islands by about 1195 and established a hereditary lordship, placing himself in turn under the protection of the Pope, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> and the Principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaea">Achaea</a>. His family ruled the islands until 1324.</p></div>
